    "result_text": "The full build passes. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: soft-duplicate flagging on owner creation\n\nWhen a newly created owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, the owner is still created and its response now carries `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nI followed the project's OfficeFloor \"one function per step, matcher-helper per concept\" idiom rather than growing an existing class:\n\n1. **`PossibleDuplicates.java`** (new matcher helper, alongside `Namesakes`/`Households`) \u2014 encapsulates the soft-match rule: same last name (case/whitespace-insensitive), same postcode, different telephone; returns the earliest matching owner's id.\n\n2. **`DetectPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new pipeline step) \u2014 reads the built `Owner`, stamps `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. It runs *after* `EnsureUniqueIdentity` (which already rejects hard duplicates with 409), so \"not a hard duplicate\" holds by construction.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step in between `countHousehold` and `save` (under the same transaction governance), so the flag is persisted and visible to both the create and the later `GET` response.\n\n4. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) fields with accessors and toString entries.\n\n5. **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns. Tests run on hsqldb + spring-data-jpa, so persistence flows through JPA/Hibernate against the new columns.\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only properties to the `Owner` response schema; MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` auto-maps the same-named fields, so no mapper change was needed.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` passes, and the full `mvn test` suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
